            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Dollar for dollar air sealing gives you more Bang for your Buck. I would look particulaly at the Chimmeny chase of your home and all electrical penetrations to the living envelope</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>Your main walls are very thin and can use some improvement. I suggest minimum of 3 inches</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>Your ceiling upgrade is limited by the size of the heel of the Truss</ceilings>
                <exposedFloors />
                <foundation>Since you have a finished basement, your only option is to dig out and insulate the  exterior. I suggest r-20 foam</foundation>
                <windows>I would look at eventually replacing the wooden basement windows</windows>
                <doors>I suggest you replace the wooden doors with metal insulated</doors>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
